                <pb facs="0267" n="233" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg233"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 189.</note>
                <head>Mr. Brent to Mr. Fish</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 241.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Lima</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-10-27"><hi rendition="#italic">Peru,
                                October</hi> 27, 1870</date>. (Received November 28,
                        1870.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that on the
                    24th instant his ex cellency President Balta issued a proclamation declaring the
                    neutrality of Peru in the existing war between France and Prussia.</p>
            </div>
